  "privacyPolicyDesc": "How the app handles permissions and data",
  "privacyPolicyIntro": "This page explains what data Dni SGGW uses, why the app needs certain permissions, and how information is handled for regular visitors and administrators.",
  "privacyPolicyLastUpdated": "Last updated: 22 April 2026",
  "privacyPolicySectionCollectedTitle": "What data the app can access",
  "privacyPolicyCollectedIntro": "Dni SGGW is designed to work without requiring an account for regular visitors, but some features rely on device permissions and cloud services.",
  "privacyPolicyCollectedCamera": "Camera access is used only to scan QR codes during the treasure hunt and related event interactions.",
  "privacyPolicyCollectedLocation": "Location access is used to verify that you are physically near a treasure hunt point before a QR code can be accepted.",
  "privacyPolicyCollectedStorage": "The app stores settings, onboarding status, notification choices, cached content, scan progress, event check-ins, and a reward device identifier locally on your device.",
  "privacyPolicyCollectedAdmin": "Administrator features use Google sign-in together with Firebase services and may store account identifiers, edited content, and uploaded images for event management.",
  "privacyPolicySectionUsageTitle": "How the data is used",
  "privacyPolicyUsageIntro": "The app uses data only to deliver the core event experience and to operate the administration tools.",
  "privacyPolicyUsageTreasureHunt": "Camera and location data are used to let visitors discover treasure hunt points, validate scans, and unlock related content.",
  "privacyPolicyUsageAppState": "Local device storage is used to remember your preferences, onboarding completion, cached data, notification choices, and scan progress between sessions.",
  "privacyPolicyUsageAdmin": "If you are an authorized administrator, sign-in data and uploaded content are used to manage timetable entries, wiki articles, treasure hunt points, and images.",
  "privacyPolicySectionSharingTitle": "Sharing and third-party services",
  "privacyPolicySharingIntro": "The app relies on Google Firebase services to provide authentication, cloud data storage, and image hosting for administration features.",
  "privacyPolicySharingFirebase": "Data submitted through administrator tools, notification token registration, and reward verification may be processed by Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Firebase Cloud Messaging, Cloud Functions, and Firebase Storage as part of operating the app.",
  "privacyPolicySharingLegal": "Information may also be disclosed if required by law or when necessary to protect the security and integrity of the service.",
  "privacyPolicySectionChoicesTitle": "Your choices",
  "privacyPolicyChoicesIntro": "You stay in control of optional permissions and locally stored app data.",
  "privacyPolicyChoicesPermissions": "You can deny camera or location permissions, but treasure hunt features that depend on them may stop working correctly.",
  "privacyPolicyChoicesAdmin": "Regular visitors do not need to create a visible account. Google sign-in is only used for approved administrator access.",
  "privacyPolicyChoicesDevice": "You can clear locally stored app data by removing the app data from your device or reinstalling the application.",
  "privacyPolicySectionContactTitle": "Contact",
  "privacyPolicyContactIntro": "If you have privacy-related questions about Dni SGGW, contact the organizers using the official event contact channels.",
  "privacyPolicyContactDetails": "Privacy-related questions should be sent through the official SGGW Days or SGGW event contact channels published with the event materials and public website.",
  "privacyPolicyContactNote": "This policy is intended to describe the current app behavior for internal testing and public event use. It should be updated whenever the app's data practices change.",
